<title>CANADA: Canada Sept bankruptcies rise over year.</title>
<headline>Canada Sept bankruptcies rise over year.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankruptcies in Canada rose to 7,632 in September from 6,603 a year earlier, the Department of Consumer and Corporate Affairs said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The department said 1,107 businesses and 6,525 consumers went bankrupt in the month.</p>
<p>In August, 7,456 bankruptcies were recorded.</p>
<p>For the year to date, 69,358 bankruptcies have been registered (10,827 businesses and 58,531 consumers), up from 57,535 in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
